course: dictionary
lesson: 811
title: Behaviour: how things act
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Behaviour is a noun. It means the way a person or animal acts, especially whether that action is good or bad, polite or rude. Read the words around it to be sure. «Good behaviour» at school earns praise, and «bad behaviour» gets a warning.
explain: Behaviour is not only for people. Scientists watch animal behaviour, such as how bees dance and how birds migrate. A machine or material can also have a behaviour, which means the way it usually acts or reacts.
explain: Look at the clues. «Strange behaviour» from a dog, like growling and a stiff body, is a warning sign, so behaviour here means how the dog acts. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "the way the dog acts" still makes sense.
fact: Behaviour means the way a person or animal acts.
fact: Behaviour can also mean the way a material, machine or animal group usually reacts.
fact: «Good behaviour» means acting well, and «bad behaviour» means acting badly.
fact: Behaviour is a noun and usually has no plural: say «good behaviour», not «good behaviours».
fact: «On your best behaviour» means trying very hard to act well.
exercise: The teacher said, «Good behaviour earns praise.» What does behaviour mean here? | A hard test | *The way a person acts, especially how well they follow the rules | A kind of weather | A type of bread
exercise: Scientists watch «animal behaviour», such as how bees dance. What is animal behaviour? | *The way animals act and react | The food an animal eats at night | The shape of an animal's body only
exercise: «One dog's behaviour tells you about that dog, not about all dogs.» What does this teach us? | Dogs never growl | All dogs behave in exactly the same way | *Each dog can behave differently, so do not judge all dogs by one dog
test: Strange behaviour from a dog, like growling and a stiff body, is a warning sign. What does behaviour mean in this sentence? | A loud noise | A kind of food | *The way an animal acts | Hair colour
test: Which phrase from this lesson means following school rules well? | animal behaviour | a behaviour chart's colour | *good behaviour | bad behaviour
exam: Mia says behaviour is a word for the shape of something. Is she right? | *No, behaviour means the way someone or something acts | Yes, it means the shape of something | Yes, it means a loud sound
